  "explainer": {
    "summary": "Ramayana: Part 1 is a Hindi-language epic film directed by Nitesh Tiwari, the first of two parts adapting Valmiki's Ramayana. It was released worldwide on November 5, 2026.",
    "why_now": "The film is still drawing attention because of its large box office run, with a reported worldwide gross of about 1,655 crore rupees, and because its sequel has reportedly been pushed back a year.",
    "background": [
      "Ranbir Kapoor plays Rama, Yash plays Ravana and Sai Pallavi plays Sita. The score is by Hans Zimmer and A. R. Rahman. Wikipedia lists a budget of 2,000 crore rupees for Part 1.",
      "Wikipedia reports mixed to positive reviews, with 78 percent on Rotten Tomatoes and 58 on Metacritic. Yash's and Sai Pallavi's Hindi dialogue drew criticism, and the filmmakers reportedly replaced some voices.",
      "Wikipedia says Part 2 has been postponed from Diwali 2027 to Diwali 2028 according to a November 2026 confirmation, and that the film is expected to stream on JioHotstar. Box office figures on that page differ slightly between its infobox and text, and the page is a secondary source."
